1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,272
My blindness is a lie because I see tomorrow bleeding through my fingertips on this cold concrete.

2
00:00:07,572 --> 00:00:15,900
A laughing woman drops her coffee, but my charcoal already shows her broken umbrella beneath a falling sign.

3
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:22,320
I grab her sleeve and scream for her to step back, but she laughs it off as crazy art.

4
00:00:22,620 --> 00:00:29,700
The heavy iron sign crashes exactly where she stood a second ago, shattering the ceramic cup.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,048
Every stroke I make steals a life from the dark and hands it back to cruel reality.

6
00:00:36,348 --> 00:00:45,708
Tonight, alone in my studio, my brush moves faster, sketching a lonely figure surrounded by flickering candles.

7
00:00:46,008 --> 00:00:52,632
I trace the fine lines of the face and realize the charcoal is leaving a wet, crimson stain.

8
00:00:52,932 --> 00:00:59,916
It is not ink or paint. It is warm, and it smells unmistakably of my own copper blood.

9
00:01:00,216 --> 00:01:06,768
I turn around slowly, feeling the cold draft of an empty room that should have no doors.

10
00:01:07,068 --> 00:01:10,572
Why are you standing so still in my canvas?
